# Reviewed exceptions to the CI secret scan.
#
# The scan deliberately over-matches: it flags any curve-prefixed key-shaped
# string, because a NEAR private key and a NEAR public key are both 64 bytes of
# base58 and cannot be told apart by shape alone. Loosening the pattern to stop
# flagging public keys would also stop it catching a leaked private one, so the
# pattern stays strict and genuine public values are listed here instead.
#
# Every entry must be a value that is public by construction. One value per
# line, with a comment saying why it is safe.

